# Testing Discipline

Every implementation phase and behavior-changing code change must include a test review.

Add or update tests when changes affect:

- services
- CLI commands
- data models or JSON artifact schemas
- validation rules
- geospatial ingestion or analysis behavior
- source status resolution
- review queue behavior
- export/report/map behavior
- error handling

Expected default command:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest
```

Run the relevant tests before committing or pushing code changes when the local environment is available.

If a change is documentation-only, tests may be unnecessary, but state that explicitly in the final summary.

If tests cannot be run, document the reason and residual risk before finishing the task.

Never implement a new feature phase without either tests for the new behavior or an explicit user-approved reason for deferring tests.
